	abstract = {The article comments on a paper by Varian in the 1982 issue of the journal which tests a finite body of data for consistency with the Generalized Axiom of Revealed Preference (GARP). The note outlines a simple and inexpensive method for calculating the approximate power of a nonparametric test of preference maximization for a simple alternative hypothesis. The power calculations in the note suggest that Varian's test of preference maximization using per capita data is quite powerful against the alternative of random behavior, but tests using aggregate data appear much less powerful.},
